# Both apps/studio and apps/docs deploy workflows run `vercel deploy` from the repo root (the
# Vercel project's own Root Directory setting handles scoping the build, but the upload step
# itself walks from cwd). The root .gitignore's build-output patterns are anchored to the repo
# root (e.g. `/.next/`), so they never exclude apps/*/.next — and those directories can hold
# multi-gigabyte Turbopack dev-cache blobs once Playwright's e2e suite has spun up a few dev
# servers, well past Vercel's 100MB per-file upload cap. Mirror the build-output excludes here,
# unanchored, so they apply at any depth regardless of which app is deploying.
node_modules
.next
.next-playground
.next-playground-local
.next-case-study
server-bin
bin
obj
test-results
playwright-report
*.tsbuildinfo
